===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In the manner of a royal [[prince]]'s conduct.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-2 Q1|II|ii|page=28|text={{...}} my appetite was not '''princely''' gote, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Arthur W. Page|title=Little Pictures of O. Henry|journal=The Book Man: An Illustrated Magazine of Literature and Life|volume=XXXVIII|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[W:Dodd, Mead & Co.|Dodd, Mead and Company]]|year=1914|section=chapter IV (The New York Days—Richard Duffy’s Narrative)|page=171|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/bookman18unkngoog/page/171/mode/1up?view=theater|passage=Oilman Hall and I tried to interest him in noticing Morgan Robertson, who was passing near the corner of Sixth Avenue and Twenty-third Street, '''princely''' dressed in a frock coat and top hat.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Paula Perry-McKay|title=Romance of a Lifetime|publisher={{w|Trafford Publishing}}|year=2005|page=172|isbn=1-4120-4343-3|passage=Ron was blithely standing at the window looking out. He was '''princely''' dressed in a black suit, and a cream-colored polo sweater. Ron turned around looking debonair as usual.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Thomas Porky McDonald|chapter=Beyond the Plate|title=Never These Men: One Man’s Look at Baseball’s Creatively Cultured Figures|location=Bloomington, Ind.; Milton Keynes|publisher={{w|AuthorHouse}}|year=2006|section=section “Tallman Tales”|page=187|passage=These are the accepted truths to all who encountered or knew of the '''princely''' dressed first sacker, whose three-piece suits and brown velvet derby defined him.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=J.L. Stewart|chapter=33|title=Avarom and the Secret of the White Mist|publisher={{w|AuthorHouse}}|year=2013|page=355|isbn=978-1-4918-0997-6|passage=“Well, the sun was barely gone and the men had dispersed. It was just me and a small squad of men, about to do our rounds when this tall '''princely''' dressed man appeared out of nowhere. He was followed by a medium built man wearing the robes of a Caravan master.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Deepa Vaibhav Shah|title=I Love... An Incomplete Commitment|publisher=Partridge India|year=2014|isbn=978-1-4828-3687-5|passage=Harmeet was a 6 feet tall sardar, good sense of humor as all sardars do. He was also very '''princely''' dressed.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Edgar Beaumont|title=Teleportkinesis|publisher=Page Publishing, Inc.|year=2017|isbn=978-1-64082-239-9|passage=She moved her big, beautiful, well-diluted eyes up and down his slender '''princely''' dressed form.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Veronica Purcell|title=The Fourth Zaldizko|series=Seriphyn Knight Chronicles|seriesvolume=book 2|publisher=Katarr Kanticles Press|year=2020|page=7|passage=The men were '''princely''' dressed in pin striped suits, fedora hats and broad toe shoes with patterned vamps. I had only seen these desirably dressed men as moving watercolor images in Velvet Rose magazines.}}

